{
  "title": "Sternoclavicular Dislocation",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/trauma/1009/sternoclavicular-dislocation",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Apr 15 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Sternoclavicular Dislocations are uncommon injuries to the chest that consist of traumatic or atraumatic dislocations of the sternoclavicular joint.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be made with plain serendipity radiographic views. CT studies are generally required to assess for direction of displacement.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is generally observation of atraumatic or chronic anterior dislocations. Closed versus open reduction is indicated for acute dislocations.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**traumatic dislocation**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "direction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "anterior (more common)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**posterior (mediastinal structures at risk)**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "important to distinguish from **medial clavicle physeal fracture** (physis doesn't fuse until age 20-25)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "mechanism",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "usually high energy injury (MVA, contact sports)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**atraumatic subluxation**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "occurs with overhead elevation of the arm",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "affected patients are younger",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "many demonstrate signs of generalized ligamentous laxity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "subluxation usually reduces with lowering the arm",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "treatment is reassurance and local symptomatic treatment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Medial clavicle",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**first bone to ossify** and **last physis to close** (age 20-25)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Sternoclavicular joint",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "osteology",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "diarthrodial saddle joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "incongruous (~50% contact)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "fibrocartilage",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "stability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "stability depends on ligamentous structures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1009/images/sternoclavicular%20anatomy%20illustration_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**posterior capsular ligament**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "most important structure for anterior-posterior stability",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**anterior sternoclavicular ligament**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "primary restraint to superior displacement of medial clavicle",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**costoclavicular (rhomboid) ligament**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "anterior fasciculus resists superior **rotation** and **lateral displacement**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "posterior fasciculus resists inferior **rotation** and **medial displacement**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**intra-articular disk ligament**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "prevents **medial displacement** of clavicle",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "secondary restraint to superior clavicle displacement",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "anterior dislocation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "deformity with palpable bump",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "posterior dislocations",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "dyspnea or **dysphagia**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "tachypnea and **stridor** worse when supine",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "palpation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "prominence that increases with arm abduction and elevation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1009/images/img_0513.jpg",
                      "caption": "Anterior sternoclavicular dislocation"
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1009/images/clinical%20photo%20-%20anterior%20dislocation%20(mediscan)_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "ROM and instability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**decreased arm ROM**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "neurovascular",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**parasthesias** in affected upper extremity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "venous congestion or diminished pulse when compared with contralateral side",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "provocative maneuvers",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "turning head to affected side may relieve pain",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP and **serendipity views**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "difficult to visualize on AP",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1009/images/Xray%20-%20AP%20-%20posterior%20dislocation_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1009/images/Xray%20-%20AP%20-%20posterior%20dislocation%203_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1009/images/Xray%20-%20AP%20-%20posterior%20dislocation%202_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**serendipity views** ( beam at 40 cephalic tilt)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1009/images/seren.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "anterior dislocation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "affected clavicle above contralateral clavicle",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "posterior dislocation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "affected clavicle below contralateral clavicle",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "study of choice",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "axial views can visualize mediastinal structures and injuries",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1009/images/CT-%20axial%20-%20posterior%20dislocation_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1009/images/CT-%20axial%20-%20posterior%20dislocation%202_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "can differentiate from **physeal fractures**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "reassurance and local symptomatic treatment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**atraumatic subluxation**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**chronic anterior dislocation that is minimally symptomatic** (> 3 weeks old)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "sling for comfort",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "return to unrestricted activity by 3 months",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "closed reduction under general anesthesia +/- thoracic surgery back-up",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "acute anterior dislocations (< 3weeks old)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "acute posterior dislocations (< 3weeks old)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "if reduction stable",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**velpeau bandage** for 6 weeks",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "may need plaster jacket or figure of eight bandage to distract shoulder",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "**elbow exercises** at 3 weeks",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "return to sports at 3 months",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "if reduction unstable",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**accept deformity** or open reduction and soft-tissue reconstruction",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**open reduction and soft-tissue reconstruction +/- thoracic surgery back-up**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1009/images/sc_joint_dislocation_1a.jpg",
                  "caption": "SC joint dislocation"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**indications**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**acute posterior dislocation with failed closed reduction**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**dysphagia**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "**shortness of breath**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "**decreased peripheral pulses**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**chronic anterior or posterior dislocation that remains persistently symptomatic**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "presence of cardiothoracic (CT) surgery is recommended",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**recent studies state that the recommendation for routine involvement of thoracic surgeons in all cases may not be necessary**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "medial clavicle excision",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "outdated procedure",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "rarely performed",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "-1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Closed reduction under general anesthesia**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "reduction technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "place patient supine with arm at edge of table and prep entire chest",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**abduct and extend** arm while applying **axial traction and direct pressure**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "simultaneously apply **direct posterior pressure** over medial clavicle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "manipulate medial clavicle with towel clip or fingers",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Open reduction and soft-tissue reconstruction**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "curvilinear incision overlying medial 1/4th of clavicle, SC joint and top of manubirum",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "care to not disrupt the SCM tendon sheath",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "clean incision through the SCJ capsule to allow for repair at the end",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "figure of 8 tendon reconstruction using 2 drill holes in the manibrium and 2 in the medial distal clavicle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "holes should be 1 cm apart to avoid cortical fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "gracilis or semitendinosus allograft/autograft most commonly used",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Medial clavicle excision**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "incision made over medial clavicle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1009/images/Clinical%20photo%20-%20intraoperative%20-%20reduction%20of%20posterior%20dislocation_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "resection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "costoclavicular ligaments must be preserved",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "preserve by resecting **< 15mm** of medial clavicle",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
